    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Anselm/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Deputy-Director--New-Hampshire-Institute-of-Politics_R1682": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, New Hampshire Institute of Politics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nSaint Anselm College, a private, liberal arts college in the Benedictine tradition, is seeking a dynamic Deputy Director for the New Hampshire Institute of Politics (NHIOP).  Reporting to the Executive Director of the NHIOP, the Deputy Director oversees the strategic, financial, supervisory, communications, and institutional leadership responsibilities. Programming, Communication and External Relations Identify strategic programming and funding opportunities Manage the overall planning, coordination and oversight of Institute programming including program selections to ensure quality and consistency while considering Institute priorities and coordinating with campus and community partners Oversee the Institute's public relations, branding, and communications, including press releases, Institute speeches, and newsletters while maintaining quality, tone, and consistency Manage speaker, special guests and donor recruitment, invitations, and correspondence to ensure a continued partnership and a positive guest experience Build and maintain relationships with authors, journalists, elected officials, publishers, community partners, special guests and vendors Coordinate the publication of Survey Center poll releases and materials, including press releases, reports, media advisories, website content, and social media Plan special events and programs in conjunction with Institute team Execute special projects as assigned by the Executive Director Maintain records of Institute traditions, events, policies, operating protocols, reference materials, exhibits, polling history, institutional archives and historical collections Leadership & Staff Supervision Provide direct supervision and performance management of the Program Assistant Oversee work planning, prioritization, and delegation of all Institute administrative responsibilities Coordinate administrative support between the Institute and the Politics Department (as managed by the faculty department chair and the Program Assistant) Oversee student interns and student intern projects with assistance from the Program Assistant Financial Management & Oversight Oversee the Institutes financial planning and forecasting of the annual operating expenses, budget development and monitoring and reporting and analysis Execute and monitor polling budgets, contracts, and consultant payments  Partner with the Finance Office on Institute finances and budgeting Qualifications Bachelor's degree preferred, along with a minimum of seven to ten years of experience in the area of public relations/communications, business and/or politics Highly motivated self-starter who takes initiative and is driven to achieve results Ability to collaborate with campus partners and external agencies and constituencies organizing and implementing Institute events and programs Attention to detail, strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines Demonstrated experience in brand management, public relations and strategic communications in a higher education, civic, nonprofit, public policy or political environment.  Supervisory and/or management experience with demonstrated ability to foster a collaborative team environment Enthusiastic, reliable team player with a commitment to excellence in customer service and professionalism Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills Budget experience preferred but not necessary Availability to work occasional evening and weekend hours for special programs or events In order to be considered for this position, please submit both a resume and a cover letter. Successful candidates will be able to assist the college to further its strategic goals for institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness ."
    },
    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Anselm/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Annual-Giving-Coordinator_R1665": {
      "title": "Annual Giving Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSaint Anselm College, a Catholic, liberal arts college in the Benedictine tradition, is seeking a highly skilled, self-motivated Annual Giving Coordinator to join the College Advancement team. Reporting directly to the Assistant Vice President of Annual Giving, the Annual Giving Coordinator will support the planning, execution, and administration of the College's annual giving program and fundraising initiatives. BASIC FUNCTION The Annual Giving Coordinator provides administrative and operational support for the Office of Annual Giving and serves as a key member of the Advancement team. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President for Annual Giving, this position works closely with the Associate Director of Annual Giving, Senior Associate Director of Annual Giving, and other Advancement colleagues to support fundraising initiatives, donor engagement efforts, stewardship activities, volunteer programs, and special projects. Serving as the primary point of contact for the Annual Giving office, the Coordinator manages a variety of administrative functions that contribute to the successful execution of annual giving strategies and programs. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong organizational skills, attention to detail, excellent customer service, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a collaborative environment. This position maintains regular interaction with alumni, donors, volunteers, students, faculty, staff, and campus partners and may require occasional evening and weekend work in support of College Advancement activities and events. CHARACTERISTIC DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Serve as the primary point of contact for the Office of Annual Giving, responding to email and phone inquiries. Provide administrative support to the Assistant Vice President of Annual Giving, and the Annual Giving team. Support the implementation of annual giving initiatives, donor engagement activities, stewardship efforts, and special projects. Maintain accurate donor and constituent records, including the entry of contact reports and other constituent information. Generate reports, lists, and data exports to support fundraising activities and departmental operations. Assist with donor communications, mailings, appeals, and other fundraising activities. Provide logistical and administrative support for events, meetings, and volunteer activities. Assist with budget administration, invoice processing, expense tracking, and financial reconciliation. Coordinate student workers and provide general office management support. Collaborate with Advancement colleagues and campus partners to support departmental goals and priorities. Attend and support Advancement events and activities as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree preferred. One to three years of experience in fundraising, annual giving, alumni relations, advancement services, higher education, nonprofit development, or a related field preferred. Experience with Blackbaud Raiser's Edge, or similar donor database systems preferred. Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel, Word, and Outlook. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, deadlines, and budgets simultaneously. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong analytical skills and attention to detail, particularly in data management and reporting. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive donor information with professionalism and discretion. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced team environment. Positive attitude and exceptional customer service skills, with demonstrated ability to engage professionally with donors, alumni, faculty, staff, students, and volunteers. Willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends in support of College events and fundraising activities. Successful candidates will be able to assist the College in furthering its strategic goals for institution-wide diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging."
    }
  },
